1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:10,450
A demo works once on your laptop. A product works thousands of times a day, on slow networks, while the AI provider is busy.

2
00:00:11,150 --> 00:00:21,350
Models do not remember. Send the conversation each time, but keep within a budget: keep the rules and the newest messages, drop the oldest.

3
00:00:23,050 --> 00:00:31,000
If the best model is busy, fall back to a smaller one, a cached answer, or a plain path without AI.

4
00:00:31,700 --> 00:00:39,550
Do not retry errors that will never succeed, like a wrong key or a bad request. Those need fixing.

5
00:00:40,250 --> 00:00:46,950
Set a timeout on every call. A clear error after thirty seconds beats waiting forever.

6
00:00:48,650 --> 00:00:59,525
When a service is busy, do not redial at once, like everyone calling a busy line. Wait one second, then two, then four, then give up kindly.

7
00:01:00,220 --> 00:01:09,770
Limit messages per user, input size and output length, and have a fallback, so the feature degrades instead of disappearing.

